  "description": "To fully remove all noncompliant façade materials, reinstate proper fire compartmentation and install new A1/A2s1, d0-rated systems that meet the requirements of Approved Document B and Regulation 7(2).\nThe remediation encompasses the complete removal and replacement of all non-compliant façade systems across the building. Works cover three primary wall types: former ACM cladding zones (Wall Type 1), areas constructed with an EPS-based insulated render system (Wall Type 2), and traditional cavity brickwork zones that contain combustible PIR insulation (Wall Type 3). Each wall type will be stripped back to an appropriate substrate level, inspected, repaired where required and rebuilt using fully compliant A1/A2s1, d0 rated systems. The works also include balcony remediation, replacement of spandrel panels and reinstatement of continuous cavity barriers. All wall types are being replaced with non combustible like for like in appearance systems.",
